<h2>5. Nature of the approval certificate</h2>
<p>When a client clicks "I approve", Signoff records the date and time (UTC), the IP address, the browser and a frozen copy of the deliverables, and generates an approval certificate.</p>
<p>This certificate is <strong>dated evidence of the client's agreement</strong> to the content shown. It is <strong>not a qualified electronic signature</strong> within the meaning of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 ("eIDAS"), nor an advanced electronic signature, and therefore does not have the legal effect equivalent to a handwritten signature that the regulation reserves for qualified signatures. Signoff does not verify the identity of the person who clicks the link: the link is sent to the email address entered by the user, and anyone who has the link can use it. In a dispute, the evidential value of the certificate is assessed by the competent court together with the other evidence.</p>
<p>Signoff is not a party to the contracts between users and their clients and gives no legal advice.</p>

